{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D(726|750|756|439)\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"8249:## D616 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council rounds 155 to 158): the period split's design v4 is accepted for a $0 scratch build; the narrow D397 departure is recorded as a reversible proposal; nothing is sent\n8471:  candidate,' not exhaustion or deferral; next, assess the paired gate-3 comparison at $0 under D439.\"\n8551:- **Round 12:** D439 permits an unchanged-request model probe; prepare it at $0.\n8597:**The complementary screen** (`reflection-6/astra/RESULT-REST.md`, $2.17; D439 about $34.7 of $40):\n8606:**Council round 17** (`reflection-6/codex-challenge-17.md`): \"CONSENSUS: Review a narrower provisional rule at $0 under D439; do not\n8613:  overrides nothing. Then a council decision under D439 records it as reversible, and a request audit follows before a probe.\n8671:**The probe** (`reflection-6/due-day/RESULT.md`, $1.71; D439 about $36.4 of $40):\n8727:- **Arms and cap:** 10 exposed topics outside the 44, 2 interleaved draws, cap $3.40 (D439 at most about $39.83).\n8742:**The run** ($1.31; D439 about $37.74): A2 wrote H20 2 of 2 and memory 2 of 2 where the frozen arm declined 2 of 2. Both arms declined\n8781:No further spend on this route. D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\n8801:D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\n8820:- **The price, stated plainly:** about $4.90 to $6.60 before retries, a cap of at least about $9, beyond D439's remaining $2.26.\n8831:- **Authority:** D426's \"no fifth Stage A is sent\" is Alex's specific decision and \"remains in force\". D439's later general delegation\n8842:- D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\n8875:    - Caps: luna $0.10 and Opus $2.15, within D439's remaining $2.26.\n8912:- **Spending:** D439 stands at about $39.29 of $40, including run-1's $0.026.\n9116:## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n9189:- **Decided** (D439; Alex active, informed):\n9287:- **Decided (D439; reversible):**\n9318:- **Decided (consensus; D439's limits):**\n9446:- **Read as:** his word to run D665's comparison once its run plan passes a council review. As D563 and D439 read \"his word\", this covers that one\n9460:## D667 · 2026-11-17 · Under D666 and D439 (council, run-plan rounds 1–10): the release comparison's run plan and the rules it takes for this run\n9494:     reviewers read \"same day\" differently, so the council took the cheaper, reversible course (D439).\n9581:- **Split, the cheaper and safer course taken (D439):**\n10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n10050:  - A verdict needs a full comparison, about $110, above D439's $40 ceiling.\n10097:- **Ceiling:** $5 on a new ledger. The estimate is about $1.4 for c8 and about $0.2 for judging. This is within D439's $40.\n10172:  - a new $2 ledger for the separating test, inside D439's $40.\n10205:    Claude, every round logged. The limits of D439 stand: the frozen ruler and the frozen production files never change, nothing is\n10206:    pushed, deployed or committed unasked, credentials and caps are untouched, and paid spend stays inside D439's $40;\n10351:- **Spend, an error of mine.** The last D439 tally was about $39.29 of $40 (D647). D679, D682 and D684 then said \"inside D439's $40\"\n10353:  - Under the two readings, D439 stands at about $39.65 (only `phase1b`, $0.36) or about $44.42 (the merge test's $2.13, `phase1` at\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11656:## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n11659:  - D439 governs: the council decides reversibly, no paid send (its ceiling is spent), nothing committed.\n11681:  is registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D750]) and built by `blind6.py`. Council round 66 reviews it before any send.\n11683:## D751 · 2026-11-23 · D750 fails on E's bracket midpoint; council 67–68 (under D439): one structural line-9 change, a paper check first, then one last writer test with an exit rule back to Alex\n11685:- **The D750 result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md`): FAIL on one settled line.\n11716:  - the test registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751]) and built by `blind7.py`: D750's design and tally, with the exit rule.\n11752:- **Pending:** Alex's answers to the two questions. Under D439 nothing paid is started.\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11814:  - the first release carries D726: number questions show their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with the range, forecast text and\n11820:- **Under D439** this is reversible: nothing is built into production, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690). It goes to Alex with\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11833:  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
