{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l AGENTS.md docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     492 AGENTS.md\n     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n    1204 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n    1101 docs/DECISIONS.md\n      87 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\n    3085 total\n     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n     6\t- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n     7\t\n     8\tOpening release work is Alex's call. This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n     9\t\n    10\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n    11\t\n    12\tA stored poc-v118 store, read-only through the service functions: `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`.\n    13\t- **19 of 47 views are number questions**: at least one rung carries a numeric `lo` or `hi`. The other 28 have no numeric band.\n    14\t- **For a number question (v8, FY2027 Data Center revenue) the service exposes the forecast in full:**\n    15\t  - `view().state`: position, label, condition, reasons, why_changed, previous_position, since_day, rounds, theme_pushes;\n    16\t  - `history()`: 75 judgements with positions and reasons, and the changes list;\n    17\t  - `changes()`: 69 rows.\n    18\t- **So today a reader sees the band and the forecast text for every number question.** The interim is not in the product.\n    19\t\n    20\t## 2. Identity: what a number question is\n    21\t\n    22\tA view is a number question when at least one of its rungs has a non-null `lo` or `hi` (`rungs` table). This is structure, an\n    23\tidentity the code can own, and it involves no judgement of importance (AGENTS §2). Yes/no and event questions have no numeric band\n    24\tand are unchanged.\n    25\t\n    26\t## 3. What a reader sees for a number question\n    27\t\n    28\t- **Shown:**\n    29\t  - the question, object, kind, what it looks at, the due day and whether it is open;\n    30\t  - the ladder: the possible bands with their labels and conditions, which define the question and state no forecast;\n    31\t  - the evidence in force with its sources, and the evidence and fact counts;\n    32\t  - the last processing check (`record()`: day and round);\n    33\t  - a marker: forecast unavailable.\n    34\t- **Withheld together:**\n    35\t  - the current band and its label and condition;\n    36\t  - the forecast text (reasons, why_changed);\n    37\t  - the previous band, since-day and round count;\n    38\t  - theme pushes;\n    39\t  - every past judgement and change.\n    40\t\n    41\t## 4. Every reader of a withheld value (searched by function and field)\n    42\t\n    43\t| Value | Written by | Read by | Change |\n    44\t|---|---|---|---|\n    45\t| `view().state` | `service.view` | `scripts/hivemind_api.py` `/views/{id}`; `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` view; `service.views` (API and MCP lists); `src/hivemind/idea.py:111` | `state` becomes `{\"forecast\": \"unavailable\"}`; `counts.rounds` is 0 |\n    46\t| `history().judgements`, `.changes` | `service.history` | API `/views/{id}/history`, MCP history | both empty for a number question; arrivals, replacements and switches kept |\n    47\t| `changes()` rows | `service.changes` | API `/changes`, MCP changes | rows of number questions dropped |\n    48\t| `evaluate()` judged_position, judged_label, judged_condition, verdict | `service.evaluate` | API `/evaluate`, MCP evaluate, `src/hivemind/idea.py:337` | judged fields null; verdict `forecast_unavailable`; `claim_position` (from the ladder alone) kept |\n    49\t| the UI's thesis state and history | `src/hivemind/bundle.py` | `poc/ui` (`prepare-data.mjs` → `src/adapters/bundle.js`) | the same rule, applied through the same function |\n    50\t| `summaries()`, `record()` | `service` | search, API, MCP | unchanged: they carry no forecast |\n    51\t\n    52\t- **One owner.** A single function in `service.py` (`is_number_question`, and a `withheld` view of a record) applied by every writer\n    53\t  above. `bundle.py` calls the same function rather than restating the rule.\n    54\t\n    55\t## 5. The switch\n    56\t\n    57\t- **The rule follows an explicit setting** passed by the launcher: `number_forecasts: \"withheld\" | \"shown\"`. It never comes from an\n    58\t  environment variable (AGENTS §3, explicit inputs).\n    59\t- The release launcher passes `withheld`. Research tools that score stored runs read the stores directly and are unaffected.\n    60\t- **Open for Alex when release work opens:** whether the default of `scripts/hivemind_api.py` and `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` becomes\n    61\t  `withheld`, which changes what the current POC page shows his colleagues.\n    62\t\n    63\t## 6. Tests (real store on a temporary path; each names its row above)\n    64\t\n    65\t- One number question and one yes/no question with judgements and evidence. For each reader in §4, the number question returns no\n    66\t  band, reasons or history and carries the marker, and the yes/no question returns exactly what it returns today.\n    67\t- **Mutants:**\n    68\t  - one reader skips the rule, and its test fails;\n    69\t  - the identity treats a yes/no question as numeric, and its test fails.\n    70\t- **The entry points as their users call them:** the API handler and the MCP tool with their defaults.\n    71\t\n    72\t## 7. The $0 reader-screen check (the first step of release work, D756)\n    73\t\n    74\t- On the stored v8 above (75 judgements, 69 changes), call every reader in §4 under `withheld`. Confirm that only the question,\n    75\t  ladder, sources, counts and the marker appear.\n    76\t- Build the UI bundle and run `poc/ui`'s page check (`verify-page.mjs`) on that thesis.\n    77\t- Expected:\n    78\t  - no band, reasons or history on the page;\n    79\t  - the evidence list intact;\n    80\t  - yes/no questions unchanged.\n    81\t\n    82\t## 8. Not in scope\n    83\t\n    84\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n    85\t- The closed v13s line.\n    86\t- Other open defects.\n    87\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
