{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'ladder_bands|legacy|before keys|does not carry bounds|no bounds' tests/test_service*.py tests/test_bundle*.py poc/ui/test/*.test.js | head -75; rg -n 'state.*current|evaluate' tests/test_service*.py | tail -25; rg -n 'seal|embedded|static' README.md | head -24; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/PROOF2F-RESULT.md | head -17\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: no matches found: tests/test_bundle*.py\n3:relationships); evaluate reads every money ladder as one partition or refuses; a corrupt record is refused.\n102:    # the non-money ladders (percentages, gigawatts) read partially or not at all, and evaluate refuses them\n104:        assert service.evaluate(ledger, view_id, '>=', 1)['evaluable'] is False\n119:def test_evaluate_judges_the_claim_against_the_judged_band(ledger):\n120:    holds = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 300e9)\n122:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 325e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n123:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 350e9)['verdict'] == 'not_yet'\n124:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '<', 350e9)['verdict'] == 'holds'\n125:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '=', 325e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'        # a band does not establish equality\n126:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>=', 300e9, '2026-05-19')['judged_position'] == 3\n128:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v17', '>=', 50e9)['verdict'] == 'borderline'\n129:    v27 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v27', '>=', 169e9)\n133:    v84 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v84', '=', 26979000000)\n135:    v70 = service.evaluate(ledger, 'v70', '>=', 500e9)\n137:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v7', '>=', 1e9)['evaluable'] is False      # a yes/no ladder has no amounts\n138:    assert service.evaluate(ledger, 'v51', '>=', 1)['evaluable'] is False       # a percentage ladder is refused, not guessed\n140:        service.evaluate(ledger, 'v3', '>', 300e9)\n32:Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/poc/mock/index.html> for the app, or <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs/system-design.html> for the design. Stop the page server with Ctrl-C. The included standalone page can browse its embedded snapshot without the API; submitting an Idea needs the service below.\n114:Then restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\n     1\t# Proof 2f: the page's day reaches the Idea call (D602), 2026-11-16, $0\n     2\t\n     3\t`poc/ui/verify-live-day.mjs` builds two check pages from the demo page `poc/mock/index.html`, whose embedded snapshot is dated\n     4\t2026-08-28. `proof2f_run.py` serves them and loads each in headless Chrome, where the checks run on load (`proof2f-output.txt`).\n     5\t`fetch` is stubbed in the existing verifiers' pattern. The library and bundles are real: they come from the ledger the stored card\n     6\twas made from (`english-v23-jev-2026-10-25`, last completed day 2026-08-15, the card's own day), through the product's `bundle`\n     7\tfunctions.\n     8\t\n     9\t- **A, the live read succeeds** (`/library` answers that ledger's library, as of 2026-08-15):\n    10\t  - the library counts the served 90 questions;\n    11\t  - the Idea is sent as of 2026-08-15;\n    12\t  - the question bundles are asked as of 2026-08-15, which exercises `readBundles`;\n    13\t  - the three chosen questions are drawn;\n    14\t  - no page error.\n    15\t- **B, the live read fails** (`/library` answers 503):\n    16\t  - the page keeps 2026-08-28 and sends the Idea as of that day;\n    17\t  - the stub answers as the real API does for a day after the store's last completed day: 409 `{\"error\": \"day not completed\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/python3 -B -c \\\"import sqlite3; from hivemind import pull; c=sqlite3.connect('file:poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1',uri=True); c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; v=c.execute(\\\\\\\"select due_day from views where view_id='v8'\\\\\\\").fetchone();print(pull.closing_reason(c,'v8',v[0],v[0]));print(c.execute(\\\\\\\"select count(*) from view_switches where not open\\\\\\\").fetchone()[0])\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
